# Architecture {id="nm-arch"}

::summary{id="nm-arch-summary"}
One TypeScript repo (`src/` is about 55k lines) holds three layers: the
**format kernel** (parser → AST → validator / renderers / patch / proof),
**Noma Cloud** (a Node HTTP server over SQLite with route modules per
resource), and the **browser app** (`web/cloud/`, bundled with esbuild).
Satellite packages (MCP server, agent SDKs, LSP) wrap the kernel. The
module-by-module reference is `docs/architecture.noma`; the layout table in
`CLAUDE.md` is the most current file map.
::

## Big picture {id="nm-arch-big-picture"}

```text
                 .noma source (Git, Cloud pages, wiki/ dirs)
                              │
                              ▼  src/parser.ts (forgiving)
                        typed AST (src/ast.ts)
        ┌──────────────┬──────┴───────┬────────────────┬──────────────┐
        ▼              ▼              ▼                ▼              ▼
  validator.ts    renderers       patch.ts          proof.ts        ids.ts
  (strict,        html, llm,      patchSource:      simulate ops,   ID/alias
  diagnostics,    json, noma,     25 block ops,     validate, hash, registry
  fixits)         markdown,       baseHash          preview
                  docx, pdf,      preconditions
                  site, paperdom,
                  slides, pptx
        └──────────────┴──────┬───────┴────────────────┴──────────────┘
                              │ used by
       ┌──────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┐
       ▼                      ▼                             ▼
   src/cli.ts           src/cloud-server.ts          packages/*
   (noma CLI)           + src/cloud/ routes          mcp-server, agent-sdk,
                        + cloud-db.ts (SQLite)       agent-sdk-py, lsp-server,
                        + blobs, collab, chat,       noma-py-seed
                          devloop, agents
                              ▲
                              │ HTTP / SSE / WebSocket (Yjs)
                        web/cloud/*.ts (browser app)
```

## Format kernel {id="nm-arch-kernel"}

The kernel follows the Iron Rules in `CLAUDE.md`: `src/ast.ts` is the
single source of truth, renderers are pure, the parser is forgiving and the
validator is strict, block IDs are public API, and examples are tests.

| Module | Role |
|---|---|
| `src/ast.ts` | Discriminated `Node` union: document, section, paragraph, code, list, list_item, quote, thematic_break, table, directive |
| `src/parser.ts` | Hand-written line-based recursive descent; fence depth by colon count (max 64); attribute grammar; heading `{id aliases}` |
| `src/inline.ts` | Lazy inline Markdown, shared `splitPipeRow` for tables |
| `src/validator.ts` | Diagnostics with spans, profiles, `--ignore-rule`, mechanical fixits |
| `src/renderer-*.ts` | HTML, LLM, JSON, `.noma`, Markdown, DOCX, site, PaperDOM; `src/pdf.ts` drives Chromium |
| `src/patch.ts` | 25 block-level ops; `patchSource` (source-preserving) is canonical |
| `src/patch-book.ts` | Book-wide transactions routed to the owning chapter |
| `src/proof.ts` | Agent safety proof: simulate, validate, hash, sandboxed preview |
| `src/ids.ts`, `src/stable-identity.ts` | ID/alias registry; persistent block, table, and cell IDs |
| `src/hash.ts` | Dependency-free sha256 behind `blockSourceHash` |
| `src/components.ts`, `src/style-tokens.ts`, `src/slides.ts` | Component kits, closed `class=` vocabulary, decks |
| `src/macros.ts` | Wiki macros (`::include`, `::excerpt`, `::children`, `::issue(s)`, `::page-properties`) as pure resolvers |
| `src/ingest-markdown.ts`, `src/confluence-*.ts`, `src/notion-import.ts` | Importers with loss reports |
| `src/cli.ts` | The `noma` command |

`src/index.ts` is the lean root npm entry: it loads no Cloud, enterprise,
or native dependencies (`PLAN.md` §24.44).

## Noma Cloud server {id="nm-arch-cloud"}

::grid{columns=2}
:::card{title="Entry and routing"}
`src/cloud-server.ts` (about 650 lines) reads config and does top-level
routing. `src/cloud/router.ts` maps `/api/:resource` to one `routes-*.ts`
module per resource (documents, sites, chat, work, devloop, agents,
approvals, enterprise, import, find, …). Shared helpers live in
`src/cloud/{http,input,context,records,render}.ts`.
:::

:::card{title="Persistence"}
`src/cloud-db.ts` (about 5,800 lines) is the SQLite store. Feature state is
split out: `cloud-chat.ts`, `cloud-devloop.ts`, `cloud-agent-ops.ts`,
`cloud-compliance.ts`, `cloud-integrations.ts`. One WAL database file is
shared by the web process and the workers.
:::

:::card{title="Attachments"}
`src/cloud-blobs.ts`: content-addressed blob store, local disk by default,
or a dependency-free SigV4 S3 driver (`NOMA_CLOUD_BLOB_STORE=s3`).
Multipart uploads in `src/cloud/multipart.ts`.
:::

:::card{title="Live co-editing"}
`src/cloud-collab.ts`: Yjs rooms with persist-before-ack, presence, and
checkpoints written back to `.noma` as normal revisions.
`src/editor-model.ts` maps `.noma` ↔ a ProseMirror-style block tree and
round-trips stable IDs. Merge granularity is the top-level block.
:::

:::card{title="Chat"}
`src/cloud/routes-chat.ts` + `src/cloud/chat.ts` + `src/cloud-chat.ts`:
channels, threads, DMs, files, reactions, read markers, SSE streams. Events
also go to a short-lived shared log so other processes can tail them.
:::

:::card{title="Dev loop"}
`src/cloud/routes-devloop.ts`, `devloop.ts`, `run-provider.ts`: GitHub
webhook (HMAC, deduped), PR/CI → issues and threads, `/deploy` and `/test`
runs on ezkeel.
:::

:::card{title="Agents"}
Scoped agent identities and the MCP/API gateway (`routes-agents.ts`),
assignments (`agent-assignments.ts`), hosted and scheduled agents
(`agent-runner.ts`, `routes-agent-ops.ts`), one approval queue
(`routes-approvals.ts`), workspace kill switch.
:::

:::card{title="AI, search, compliance"}
`cloud-llm.ts` (Claude Messages API over fetch, fake provider),
`cloud-embeddings.ts` (local hash default, OpenAI-compatible, Voyage),
`cloud-platform.ts` (RAG, trust, recipes, policy), `routes-find.ts` (⌘K),
`dlp.ts` and `siem.ts` (DLP detectors, audit NDJSON to a SIEM).
:::
::

Other Cloud modules: `src/cloud/oidc.ts` (native OIDC login),
`src/cloud-git-sync.ts` (`noma cloud export-space|sync`),
`src/cloud/integrations.ts` + `src/slack-import.ts` + `src/jira-import.ts`
(switching), `src/cloud-templates.ts`, `src/zip.ts`.

Background work runs in-process on a timer, or in the standalone workers
under `apps/worker/` (`cloud-queue.ts`, `cloud-maintenance.ts`).

## Browser app {id="nm-arch-web"}

`web/cloud/` holds about 50 modules for the Cloud UI: `main.ts` (listeners
and boot), `state.ts` (one shared state object), `api.ts`, `navigation.ts`,
`editor.ts` and `visual-editor.ts` (ProseMirror), `visual-collab.ts` (Yjs),
`chat.ts`, `work.ts`, `devloop.ts`, `palette.ts` (⌘K), `admin.ts`, and more.
`web/workbench.ts` is the standalone editor with the proof panel.
`scripts/build-web-ui.ts` bundles them with esbuild into `site/assets/`, and
`npm run typecheck:web` checks them against `tsconfig.web.json`.

The landing page `site/index.html` is hand-written HTML, not rendered from
`.noma`.

## Packages {id="nm-arch-packages"}

| Package | What it is |
|---|---|
| `packages/mcp-server` | `@ferax564/noma-mcp-server`: stdio MCP with `read_doc`, `list_ids`, `validate_doc`, `patch_block` |
| `packages/agent-sdk` | `@ferax564/noma-agent-sdk`: TS workflow layer (safe patch, capability checks, transcript replay) |
| `packages/agent-sdk-py` | Python agent SDK starter |
| `packages/noma-py-seed` | Native Python second implementation seed: parser, ids, 3 patch ops against the conformance corpus |
| `packages/lsp-server` | `@ferax564/noma-lsp`: diagnostics, symbols, definition, completion; bundled by `tools/vscode-noma/` |
| `packages/{document-core,work,platform,…}` | Enterprise extraction boundaries. They re-export the CLI kernel and add no isolation yet (`docs/review-2026-09.md` §5) |

## PaperDOM fork {id="nm-arch-paperdom"}

`src/paperdom-*.ts` is a maintained fork of the MIT-licensed PaperDOM
canvas/slide kernel. `src/paperdom-pin.ts` records the base repo and commit
for provenance. Since 2026-09-24 the fork is type-checked and linted like
the rest of `src/` (maintainer decision 4 in `docs/strategy-2026-09.md` §8).
It backs `--to paperdom`, `::canvas` (`src/canvas-svg.ts`), `--to pptx`
(`src/paperdom-pptx.ts`), and canvas → `.noma` sync
(`src/paperdom-sync.ts`).

## Public entry points {id="nm-arch-barrels"}

| Import | File | Loads |
|---|---|---|
| `@ferax564/noma-cli` | `src/index.ts` | Kernel only |
| `@ferax564/noma-cli/cloud` | `src/cloud.ts` | Cloud server and store; needs `better-sqlite3` |
| `@ferax564/noma-cli/enterprise` | `src/enterprise.ts` | Enterprise Docs / Visuals / Work kernel (`src/enterprise-*.ts`) |

The enterprise modules include real code and design spikes. Treat
`docs/enterprise.noma` as the authority on which parts are implemented and
which remain open.

## Where to change what {id="nm-arch-change-guide"}

| Change | Start in | Also touch |
|---|---|---|
| New directive name | a renderer case in `src/renderer-html.ts` | `docs/spec.noma`, an example, validator rule if it has invariants |
| New AST node variant | `src/ast.ts` | every renderer switch, parser, tests (`CLAUDE.md` checklist) |
| New patch op | `src/patch.ts` | `schemas/patch-op.schema.json`, conformance fixture, RFC |
| New Cloud API resource | new `src/cloud/routes-*.ts` | one entry in `src/cloud/router.ts` |
| New Cloud UI panel | `web/cloud/` | `npm run build:web-ui`, `typecheck:web` |
